edges are loops, is a clique of"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"one. The order is Eppstein–Löffler–Strash’s: by the cliques’ first vertex in"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"coreNumbers().degeneracyOrdering"},{"type":"text","text":", then as Bron–Kerbosch with Tomita’s pivot (ties to the least"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"index) and branches in ascending index meets them. The sequence holds the graph, so iterating"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"again gives the same cliques. O(n + m) before the first clique, O(d·n·3^(d\/3)) in all for"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"degeneracy d."}],"type":"topic"},"doc://Cliques/documentation/Cliques/MaximalCliques/reductions(_:)":{"abstract":[],"role":"symbol","type":"topic","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"func"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"reductions"},{"kind":"text","text":"(("},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"Self"},{"kind":"text","text":"."},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"Element","preciseIdentifier":"s:ST7ElementQa"},{"kind":"text","text":", "},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"Self"},{"kind":"text","text":"."},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"Element","preciseIdentifier":"s:ST7ElementQa"},{"kind":"text","text":") "},{"kind":"keyword","text":"throws"},{"kind":"text","text":" -> "},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"Self"},{"kind":"text","text":"."},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"Element","preciseIdentifier":"s:ST7ElementQa"},{"kind":"text","text":") "},{"kind":"keyword","text":"rethrows"},{"kind":"text","text":" -> ["},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"Self"},{"kind":"text","text":"."},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"Element","preciseIdentifier":"s:ST7ElementQa"},{"kind":"text","text":"]"}],"kind":"symbol","url":"\/documentation\/cliques\/maximalcliques\/reductions(_:)","title":"reductions(_:)","identifier":"doc:\/\/Cliques\/documentation\/Cliques\/MaximalCliques\/reductions(_:)"}}}